egy, therefore, is to open with the straight `♦9 ♣10 ♥J ♥Q ♠K ♦A`, guaranteeing an advantageous position and efficiently clearing the weaker cards. This leaves a clean path to finish the hand with Full Houses and the Rocket. No hesitation. Let\'s do this.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The current hand is strong, featuring a Rocket (Red Joker + Black Joker), two triplets (555, 777), and several pairs (44, 88, 1010, KK). The main challenge is dealing with the isolated single cards: 9, J, Q, A. The most efficient strategy is to form a straight using these singles. The straight 9-10-J-Q-K-A (6 cards) is ideal because it consumes the problematic singles (9, J, Q, A) and breaks two pairs (10s and Ks) into singles, which is a worthwhile trade-off. This creates a remaining hand structure of two Full Houses (555+44 and 777+88), two singles (10, K), and the Rocket. Comparing this to the 8-card straight option (7-A), the 6-card straight is superior because it preserves the 777 and 88 for a Full House, whereas the 8-card straight would break them into less efficient components (pair and single). Furthermore, the straight 9-10-J-Q-K-A is Ace-high, meaning it cannot be beaten by any other straight, guaranteeing you maintain the initiative (unless bombed).\n\nReason: Playing the straight 9-10-J-Q-K-A is the optimal move to restructure the hand. It clears the difficult single cards (9, J, Q, A) while forming the highest possible straight of its length, securing the lead. This leaves a coherent set of Full Houses and high cards backed by a Rocket.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦9", "♣10", "♥J", "♥Q", "♠K", "♦A"]}'}
